<body>
    <h1>User Story =E2=80=94 Instructions &amp; Scaffold</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h2 id=3D"UserStory=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-PHASE1=E2=80=
=94PLAN">PHASE 1 =E2=80=94 PLAN</h2>
<h3 id=3D"UserStory=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-Step1=E2=80=94InputCh=
ecklist">Step 1 =E2=80=94 Input Checklist</h3>
<p>Confirm you have each input. Source can be a document, Confluence page, =
or chat response.</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-layout=3D"default" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>#</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Input</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Status</p></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>1</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Feature detail =E2=80=94 rules, validations, formulas, edge cases</p></t=
d>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>ok / partial / missing</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>2</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Users and personas</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>ok / partial / missing</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>3</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Parent epic and user journey step</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>ok / partial / missing</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>4</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Screen and UI context</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>ok / missing</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>5</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>NFRs</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>ok / partial / missing</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<ul>
<li>
<p>missing =E2=80=94 ask the user before planning</p></li>
<li>
<p>partial =E2=80=94 proceed and flag the gap in Questions</p></li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> This scaffold assumes your project uses an EpicCo=
de naming convention (e.g. INV-F01). Adjust the Feature ID format, Document=
 Reference format, and story naming to match your project's conventions if =
different.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3 id=3D"UserStory=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-Step2=E2=80=94AskACfo=
rmat">Step 2 =E2=80=94 Ask AC format</h3>
<p>Only after inputs are confirmed as ok or partial, ask:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">What fo=
rmat for acceptance criteria?
1. Given / When / Then
2. The system must...</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"UserStory=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-Step3=E2=80=94PlanFor=
mat">Step 3 =E2=80=94 Plan Format</h3>
<p>If the user provides a full PRD with multiple features, present one comb=
ined plan for all features and wait for a single approval before generating=
.</p>
<p>You must use exactly this format and no other. Produce this plan and sto=
p. Wait for PM approval before generating.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">USER ST=
ORY PLAN =E2=80=94 [Feature Name] ([Feature ID])
AC format: [chosen]

WHAT I UNDERSTOOD
[2-3 sentences =E2=80=94 what this feature does, who uses it, which screen]

STORIES I WILL WRITE
1. [Title] =E2=80=94 [happy path / validation / edge case]
2. [Title] =E2=80=94 [happy path / validation / edge case]

TBC SECTIONS =E2=80=94 BLOCKED
[List every TBC section in the source PRD that affects this feature. For ea=
ch: state the section, what is missing, and that stories for this area will=
 not be generated until resolved. If none: "None =E2=80=94 all sections res=
olved."]

QUESTIONS BEFORE I PROCEED
[Genuine blockers only. If none: "None =E2=80=94 ready to proceed."]

WAITING FOR APPROVAL =E2=80=94 reply APPROVED to continue, or tell me what =
to change.</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Do not generate any stories until the user replies APPROVED. If changes =
requested, revise and wait again.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"UserStory=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-PHASE2=E2=80=94EXECUT=
E">PHASE 2 =E2=80=94 EXECUTE</h2>
<p>Only begin this phase after receiving approval in Phase 1.</p>
<h3 id=3D"UserStory=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-Rules">Rules</h3>
<p><strong>Story quality:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Persona must be specific =E2=80=94 never "user"</p></li>
<li>
<p>One goal per story =E2=80=94 if you write "and", split it</p></li>
<li>
<p>Value must be observable =E2=80=94 "better experience" is not value</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p>Each story must be completable by one developer in 1-3 days =E2=80=94 sp=
lit if larger</p></li>
<li>
<p>When splitting a story: (a) happy path in one story, (b) validation and =
errors in a second, (c) edge cases in a third</p></li>
<li>
<p>Every story must pass INVEST: Independent, Negotiable, Valuable, Estimab=
le, Small, Testable</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Each AC on its own numbered line</p></li>
<li>
<p>Always include: happy path, validation failure, empty state</p></li>
<li>
<p>Testable =E2=80=94 "displays error message X below field Y" not "shows a=
n error"</p></li>
<li>
<p>Group related validation failures on the same screen into one story with=
 multiple ACs =E2=80=94 not one story per failure condition</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Edge cases =E2=80=94 always consider:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>First-time use (no existing data)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Maximum data volume</p></li>
<li>
<p>Invalid or missing input</p></li>
<li>
<p>Accessibility (keyboard navigation, screen reader)</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>NFRs:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>NFRs from PRD apply to all stories in this feature</p></li>
<li>
<p>Do not repeat NFRs as user stories</p></li>
<li>
<p>Reference PRD in the Related Pages table</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Data Dictionary:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Populate only if the feature involves data entry, calculation, or valida=
tion</p></li>
<li>
<p>Leave empty and mark N/A for display-only or navigation features</p></li=
>
</ul>
<p><strong>Content:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Do not invent fields, screens, or behaviours =E2=80=94 flag as TBC if un=
certain</p></li>
<li>
<p>Follow the approved plan exactly</p></li>
<li>
<p>If the source PRD contains TBC sections relevant to the feature being wr=
itten, flag them in the Questions table with status Open and do not generat=
e stories for those areas =E2=80=94 add a note in the Stories table: "Stori=
es for [area] not generated =E2=80=94 PRD section TBC. Resolve before gener=
ating."</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"UserStory=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-Output">Output</h3>
<p>After generating all feature stories, output them in full in chat. Do no=
t summarise. Do not truncate. The user must be able to read all stories bef=
ore verification begins.</p>
<p>Then immediately proceed to Phase 3 =E2=80=94 Verify. Do not wait for us=
er input before running Verify.</p>
<h3 id=3D"UserStory=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-Scaffold">Scaffold</h=
3>
<p>The scaffold below is for ONE feature. If the PRD has multiple features,=
 generate a separate complete scaffold instance for each feature. Do not co=
mbine features into one scaffold.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"UserStory=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-Overview">Overview</h=
2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-layout=3D"default" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Attribute</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Detail</p></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Initiative</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>[from source material or ask user if not present]</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Epic</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>[Epic Name]</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Feature ID</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>[EpicCode]-F01</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Feature Name</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>[Feature Name]</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Document Reference</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>US-[EpicCode]-[sequence]</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Document Owner</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>[Name]</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Priority</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Must Have / Should Have / Could Have</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Status</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Draft</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"UserStory=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-Contents">Contents</h=
2>
<p>[Insert Table of Contents macro here after publishing]</p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"UserStory=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-1.FeatureOverview">1.=
 Feature Overview</h2>
<p>[What this feature does, which screen it lives on, which persona uses it=
, and which step in the parent epic journey it appears at =E2=80=94 one par=
agraph.]</p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"UserStory=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-2.DataDictionary">2. =
Data Dictionary</h2>
<p>N/A =E2=80=94 or populate if feature involves data entry, calculation, o=
r validation.</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-layout=3D"default" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Field / Data Point</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>ID</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Screen</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Type</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Mandatory</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Default</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Validation / Derivation</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Error Message</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Notes</p></th>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"UserStory=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-3.UserStories">3. Use=
r Stories</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-layout=3D"default" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Story</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>User Story</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Acceptance Criteria</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>UI Notes</p></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>[Jira-ready title]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>As a [persona], I want [action] so that [benefit].</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC 1: [criterion] AC 2: [criterion] AC 3: [edge case]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>[Screen / note]</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"UserStory=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-4.Questions">4. Quest=
ions</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-layout=3D"default" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>#</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Question</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Area</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Owner</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Date Raised</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Answer</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Answered By</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Answered Date</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Status</p></th>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>Status values: Open / Answered / Deferred / No longer relevant</p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"UserStory=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-5.RelatedPagesandSour=
ceDocuments">5. Related Pages and Source Documents</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-layout=3D"default" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Page</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Link</p></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Parent PRD</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Project Rules</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p></p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"UserStory=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-PHASE3=E2=80=94VERIFY=
ANDPUBLISH">PHASE 3 =E2=80=94 VERIFY AND PUBLISH</h2>
<p>This phase is mandatory. It must run immediately after Execute =E2=80=94=
 do not wait for user input to begin.</p>
<h3 id=3D"UserStory=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-Step1=E2=80=94Verify"=
>Step 1 =E2=80=94 Verify</h3>
<p>Run every check below immediately after outputting the stories. Report t=
he result of every single check out loud =E2=80=94 do not summarise or skip=
 any:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">USER ST=
ORY VERIFICATION =E2=80=94 [Epic Name]

| Check | Pass / Fail | Issue |
|---|---|---|

DOCUMENT SETUP
| Feature ID follows [EpicCode]-F0n format | | |
| Document Reference follows US-[EpicCode]-[sequence] format | | |
| Contents placeholder present after Overview table | | |
| Each feature has its own separate scaffold =E2=80=94 features are not com=
bined | | |

COMPLETENESS
| All features from PRD present =E2=80=94 none dropped or skipped | | |
| Data Dictionary populated for data-entry features =E2=80=94 N/A for other=
s | | |
| Questions flagged =E2=80=94 not silently assumed | | |
| TBC sections from PRD flagged in Questions table and stories withheld =E2=
=80=94 not silently skipped | | |

CONTENT ACCURACY
| No invented fields, screens, or behaviours | | |
| Every story references a confirmed persona =E2=80=94 never "user" | | |
| No NFRs written as user stories | | |

STRUCTURE AND FORMAT
| AC format matches chosen format throughout | | |
| Each AC on its own numbered line | | |
| Happy path, validation failure, empty state covered for every feature | |=
 |
| Related validation failures grouped =E2=80=94 not split into separate sto=
ries | | |
| Every AC is specific and testable | | |
| Story titles suitable for Jira import | | |

STANDARDS
| Each story passes INVEST | | |
| Project Rules applied =E2=80=94 naming conventions followed | | |

OVERALL: PASS / FAIL
Issues to fix: [section =E2=80=94 specific fix needed]</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>If overall result is FAIL: fix every failing item, output the corrected =
stories in full in chat, and re-run the full checklist.</p>
<p>If overall result is PASS, end with this exact line: <br>
"VERIFY PASSED =E2=80=94 reply PUBLISH to create the pages, or let me know =
if you want to make any changes first."</p>
<p>Do not proceed to Step 2 until the user replies PUBLISH or gives clear c=
onfirmation.</p>
<h3 id=3D"UserStory=E2=80=94Instructions&amp;Scaffold-Step2=E2=80=94Publish=
">Step 2 =E2=80=94 Publish</h3>
<p>CRITICAL =E2=80=94 Each feature must be published as its own separate pa=
ge. Never combine multiple features into a single page. If there are 4 feat=
ures in the PRD, there must be 4 separate pages created.</p>
<p>Only after the user confirms PUBLISH:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Ask the user: "Which page should these user stories be published under? =
Please share the page URL or page title."</p></li>
<li>
<p>Immediately upon receiving the URL or title, do not ask for a second con=
firmation of the path.</p></li>
<li>
<p>For each feature =E2=80=94 one at a time: <br>
a. Create a new page titled "[FeatureID] =E2=80=94 [Feature Name]" under th=
e specified parent page <br>
b. Publish only that feature's content to that page <br>
c. Share the URL for that page before moving to the next feature <br>
d. Repeat for every remaining feature</p></li>
<li>
<p>After all features are published, end with: <br>
"ALL STORIES COMPLETE =E2=80=94 [list each URL on its own line]. Ready for =
Jira import. Note: add the Table of Contents macro in the Contents section =
of each page to enable navigation."</p></li>
</ol>
<p>Do not mark the session complete until every feature has its own publish=
ed page and every URL is shared.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
